n_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.025793323520390456,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":39.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.00884798009584098,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":61.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01315844134263875,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.59358,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Pioneer Bancorp, Inc. operates as a holding company for Pioneer Bank, National Association that provides various banking products and services in New York. It accepts various deposit accounts, such as demand, savings, and money market accounts, as well as certificates of deposit accounts. The company's loan products include commercial real estate, commercial and industrial, commercial construction, residential mortgage, consumer loans, home equity loans, and lines of credit. It also invests in securities, including U.S. treasury securities, fixed-rate mortgage-backed securities and collateralized mortgage obligations, fixed-rate investment grade bonds, and corporate debt securities. In addition, the company offers personal and commercial insurance products, including homeowners, automobile, and comprehensive business insurance; employee benefit products and consulting services, such as group health, dental, disability, and life insurance products; defined contribution and benefit administration, and human resource management services; and wealth management services comprising investment advice, retirement income planning, estate planning, business succession, and employer retirement planning. Pioneer Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1889 and is based in Albany, New York. Pioneer Bancorp, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Pioneer Bancorp MHC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas L. Amell | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 296 people. Revenue per employee of $325K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Pioneer Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $438M market cap on $96M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 59% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 79% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7948813250427447},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to PBFS Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/Technical_Reactions_to_PBFS_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111226111002_1794543002.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794543002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Pioneer Bancorp (NASDAQ:PBFS) and Byline Bancorp (NYSE:BY)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/reviewing-pioneer-bancorp-nasdaqpbfs-and-byline-bancorp-nyseby.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794453302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Survey: Pioneer Bancorp (NASDAQ:PBFS) and Banco Bradesco (NYSE:BBD)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/financial-survey-pioneer-bancorp-nasdaqpbfs-and-banco-bradesco-nysebbd.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794338151.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":